{:doc ["New-DSL conversion of ac/vfx/effects/screen_flash_session.edn (S6)."
        "The old :control-graph was already an empty :vfx/timeline (:children"
        "[]) -- this effect's :inputs (alpha/duration/color) are presentation-"
        "side-channel data consumed directly by the client HUD overlay, never"
        "by the geometry sampler at all, so an empty :scene is an exact port,"
        "not the \"confirmed-dead component\" case the other empty-:scene files"
        "in this pass are (see blood_retrograde_charge.edn's docstring)."
        "Generic presentation side channel; intensity, duration and color are"
        "supplied by the signal and are not tied to any skill. A screen-space"
        "overlay is inherently first-person-only -- broadcasting it would flash"
        "nearby players' screens, not the caster's."]
 :schema-version 1
 :kind :vfx/system
 :asset/type :vfx/system
 :asset/version 1
 :id :screen-flash-session
 :revision 1
 :lifecycle :transient
 :audience {:scope :self}
 :inputs {:spawn {:alpha :float :duration-ticks :int :color :any}
          :update {:alpha :float}
          :destroy {}}
 :state-slots {:age :float}
 :scene
 "{:ability :screen-flash-session
   :do [(finish {:outcome :performed})]}"}
